                  <provenance type="#e b" source="6864"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_360">Malmesbury,
                        Wiltshire. Benedictine Abbey of St Mary the Virgin and St Aldhelm</orgName><p>'Malmesbur'' on flyleaf pasted to fol. iiv, above which is the
                        number 'xvj' and below a table of contents (all in one hand, s. xiv
                        ex.).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">In Oxford in the fifteenth century, when it
                     was deposited in the Selton chest, 17 July [....]. Given to Merton by John
                     Gigur, formerly warden, in 1486.</provenance>
               <provenance source="8308"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_435">Oxford, Oxfordshire. Merton
                        College</orgName><p>‘Made at Malmesbury Abbey for William of Malmesbury
                        (d. c. 1143). [. . .] Given to the College by [John] Gygur [. . .]. The
                        donation was made in July 1486 (Registrum, p. 79).’ (Thomson, Merton,
                        135)</p></provenance>
